/** What had to be resolved before this list could be seeded honestly. */
export const HURFORDS_SOLID_AUDIT: { topic: string; note: string }[] = [
  { topic: "The grade is punched out of the product code", note: "520 codes print a literal '##' and 9 print a single '#' where the two-letter grade code belongs. Substituting the row's own grade code into either produces a 13-character code, and doing it across the whole list gives 552 codes with ZERO collisions, so the single hash is a one-character typo in the same template slot rather than a different kind of gap. The 9 are FETRI#080019 (Thermally Enhanced Red Ironbark, 3 grades) and FPTU3#083014 / FPTU3#085014 (Turpentine, 3 grades each). The resolved code is what goes on an order; the printed template is kept beside it so an invoice can be matched either way. 24 rows print a full code with no placeholder at all: the 2 Sports Floor rows, the 6 Cypress Pine rows and the 15 XL Parquetry rows, all of which are single-grade lines." },
  { topic: "Solid prices by the lineal metre, engineered prices by the m2", note: "Both columns are printed and they agree: $/LM over the board width in metres matches the printed $/m2 to within 0.5% on all 495 board rows that print both, with 0 exceptions. LM is the unit Hurford's sell on and the pack size is quoted in LM, so LM is seeded as the unit with the board width carried in widthM so the app can show m2 as well. This is the opposite of Hurford's engineered list, which prices per m2, and the difference is real rather than a presentation choice." },
  { topic: "Parquetry prices per m2 and sells by the box", note: "All 57 parquetry rows print a $/m2 and no $/LM, because a parquetry block has no lineal run. XL Parquetry is 12 boards a box (1.014 m2, or 0.983 m2 on the 640mm rows). Block Hardwood Parquetry is 84 pieces / 1.420 m2 a box at 14mm and 60 pieces / 1.014 m2 at 19mm, with the BOX PRICE printed in the notes on all 42 rows. Every printed box price reconciles to the rate times the printed m2 a box: 36 of the 42 land on the cent and the other 6 land a single cent off, because the m2 a box Hurford's print is itself rounded. So the box price is carried as a cross-check and the m2 rate stays the seeded one." },
  { topic: "Row 510 is a heading, not a product", note: "Its Product Code reads '650 x 128 x 14 XL Parquetry' with no species, no $/LM, no $/m2 and no pack size, and the two rows beneath it are the real 650 x 128 x 14 boards. It is dropped, taking 553 rows to 552. It is also the list's only blank Species / Colour cell, so that gap is explained rather than outstanding." },
  { topic: "Two XL Parquetry rows print the wrong length", note: "Roasted Peat and Roasted Cayenne sit under a '650 x 128 x 14' size column, but the species text says 640mm, the code ends 64 rather than 65, and 12 boards of 640 x 128 is the printed 0.983 m2 a box where 650 would give 0.998. The length is taken as 640mm on the strength of the code and the box m2 agreeing. Worth telling Hurford's the size column is wrong." },
  { topic: "Cypress Pine 62 x 20 has no price", note: "Row 491, FECYPN062020, prints neither a $/LM nor a $/m2 where the other five Cypress sizes print both, and its box and pack-price cells are empty too. It is seeded price-on-application with a 600 L/M pack size, which IS printed, rather than dropped or filled in from the neighbouring 85 x 20. Ask Hurford's whether the size is still made." },
  { topic: "109 rows print no pack size, and that is the product, not a gap", note: "Overlay T&G 83 x 12 (53 rows) and Overlay T&G FOURTEEN+ 85 x 14 (56 rows) are blank in the Approx Pack Size column while every other board size in those ranges prints one: 83 x 14 is 400 LM, 130 x 14 is 300, 180 x 14 is 200, Ultra10 86 x 12 is 400. ANSWERED BY DAMIEN: they are natural timber supplied in random lengths from 1 metre to 6 metres, so there is no fixed pack quantity to print. Left null on purpose and quoted by the lineal metre, NOT assumed to be 400. A quote on these cannot state a pack count, and because Hurford's yard freight is priced per pack, a yard or depot delivery of these has to be quoted by Hurford's directly." },
  { topic: "A species name is misspelled on 8 rows", note: "'Thermally Enhances Red Ironbark' appears on Traditional T&G at 80 x 19, 130 x 19 and 180 x 21, while the correct 'Thermally Enhanced Red Ironbark' appears across the Overlay ranges. There is no correctly-spelled rival at those three sizes for it to be confused with, so it is the same product with a typo. The price book carries the corrected name and the row keeps the source spelling for matching an invoice." },
  { topic: "What the printed freight figures actually cost Terra", note: "The rules sheet prints $80 + GST the first pack then $15 + GST a pack thereafter to a yard or depot, a crane truck to site at $320 + GST (Brisbane / Gold Coast) or $450 + GST (Sunshine Coast), a $80 + GST job lot fee for less than full pack quantities, and for boxed parquetry a $150 broken pack fee plus a $150 freight fee with a note that a $80 freight surcharge also applies. DAMIEN HAS CUT THROUGH IT: delivery INTO TERRA'S WAREHOUSE IS FREE, because Terra unload with their own forklift and need no crane truck or tailgate. So on a warehouse order the per-pack freight, the crane truck and the parquetry freight fee are all $0, and the only thing that lands is the handling: the $80 job lot fee on a short order, and on boxed parquetry the $150 broken pack fee instead. TO SITE the charge is a FLAT $320 + GST a delivery with the crane truck, whatever the load. THE $450 SUNSHINE COAST RATE IS NOT RELEVANT TO TERRA and is recorded for reference only, never auto-applied. The printed $80/$15 per-pack yard freight is likewise recorded but never auto-applied, since it describes a depot delivery Terra does not buy." },
  { topic: "Terra's own 10 m2 delivery rule is Terra's, not Hurford's", note: "The rules sheet states it plainly: up to 10 m2 defaults to Terra collecting to the shop at $0 Hurford freight, over 10 m2 defaults to the $320 crane truck to site, the threshold is a Terra operational rule and not a Hurford published one, and it applies to Hurford SOLID flooring only. It is carried as guidance for the office, overridable per order, and never as an automatic charge." },
  { topic: "Price age", note: "Effective 12 February 2026, about seven months old at seed time and the freshest of the three Hurford's lists. Seeded as it stands." },
];

